Backport of vLLM PR #62318 (head e5b2296947d5160cc3edcbb630abea2512be5e02)
onto v0.32.0, source files only (the PR's unit test and Buildkite change are
not part of the installed package and are left out).

Upstream-PR: vllm-project/vllm#62318
Upstream-Issue: vllm-project/vllm#62308
Remove-When: a vLLM release used as BASE_IMAGE contains the merged fix for
  #62308 (PR #62318 or whatever replaces it). Not before: a merged PR that
  is not yet in a release tag still needs this patch.

[Bugfix][Model] Qwen3.8-Flash-Next: load checkpoints with quantized q/k/v and
a BF16 QSA indexer

Since #59533 (first released in v0.32.0) the class-level
packed_modules_mapping["qkv_proj"] of Qwen4ExpForCausalLM lists
indexer.index_qk_proj. Quant configs read that mapping before the model is
built, so they check q/k/v and the QSA indexer as one fused layer, and
checkpoints that quantize q/k/v but keep the indexer in BF16 fail with:

  ValueError: Found different quantization schemes for the shards of
  language_model.model.layers.3.self_attn.qkv_proj. vLLM requires all to
  use the same scheme.

Keep the indexer out of the mapping the quant config sees, and fuse it into
qkv_proj only when both resolve to the same quant method and scheme.

Rebased by 3-way cherry-pick: the qsa.py hunk's context moved on main
(#60602 extended the use_fused_qsa_prepare condition just above it); the
changed lines are identical to the PR's.

Original-Author: Seungryong Kim <137975233+srkim-business@users.noreply.github.com>

